1
00:00:44,156 --> 00:00:45,496
(Episode 3)

2
00:01:08,016 --> 00:01:09,616
My age this year.

3
00:01:12,156 --> 00:01:14,856
I will be 60 before I know it.

4
00:01:19,096 --> 00:01:22,126
I still wanted to keep a few photos of him.

5
00:01:22,996 --> 00:01:24,896
We only lived together for a few years,

6
00:01:25,836 --> 00:01:28,136
but he was still my dad for a little while.

7
00:01:29,476 --> 00:01:31,576
The dad who raised me is still my dad.

8
00:01:32,576 --> 00:01:35,176
She might not be very affectionate,

9
00:01:35,246 --> 00:01:39,586
but either way, Da Mi is the best out of the three.

10
00:01:40,686 --> 00:01:43,416
You did a good thing taking her in back then.

11
00:01:45,856 --> 00:01:47,386
It was more than just a good thing.

12
00:01:48,826 --> 00:01:50,896
She saved my life, Mother.

13
00:01:52,626 --> 00:01:54,196
Dear, what is wrong?

14
00:01:54,266 --> 00:01:55,665
I know you are angry,

15
00:01:55,666 --> 00:01:57,636
but where are you going at this hour?

16
00:01:57,696 --> 00:02:01,936
Do not try to stop me, Mom. Please let go of me.

17
00:02:02,206 --> 00:02:05,136
I am not living with that man anymore.

18
00:02:08,546 --> 00:02:11,816
You must endure it for the sake of the kids. What can you do?

19
00:02:12,016 --> 00:02:16,056
I will break his legs and make him stay put if I have to,

20
00:02:16,116 --> 00:02:18,116
so just bear with it for tonight, okay?

21
00:02:19,326 --> 00:02:20,925
As if coming home with his underwear inside out...

22
00:02:20,926 --> 00:02:21,956
wasn't bad enough,

23
00:02:22,156 --> 00:02:23,425
yesterday he stayed out all night...

24
00:02:23,426 --> 00:02:25,226
and came home wearing a brand-new pair he'd bought.

25
00:02:25,356 --> 00:02:28,396
And you're still telling me to just put up with it?

26
00:02:28,896 --> 00:02:30,995
He said he bought new ones...

27
00:02:30,996 --> 00:02:32,706
because he got drunk and wet himself.

28
00:02:33,036 --> 00:02:36,306
You know, at the convenience store.

29
00:02:37,106 --> 00:02:38,876
Do you really expect me to believe that?

30
00:02:40,506 --> 00:02:44,146
I told him to bring the woman home if he plans to live with her,

31
00:02:44,216 --> 00:02:47,286
and I would give him a divorce then.

32
00:02:48,686 --> 00:02:52,826
If he is going to sleep around, he should at least not get caught.

33
00:02:53,156 --> 00:02:55,556
How can he go crazy for every woman he sees...

34
00:02:55,626 --> 00:02:56,695
and sleep with them?

35
00:02:56,696 --> 00:02:58,556
He does not even seem human.

36
00:02:59,966 --> 00:03:02,026
I am sorry, Mother.

37
00:03:03,296 --> 00:03:04,536
Take care of yourself.

38
00:03:08,266 --> 00:03:09,906
Dear.

39
00:03:09,976 --> 00:03:11,006
Mi Mi!

40
00:03:12,976 --> 00:03:15,776
Of all the things to inherit from his father,

41
00:03:15,846 --> 00:03:18,076
he has to chase women whenever he gets the chance.

42
00:03:18,716 --> 00:03:22,346
He is always making that sweet girl cry.

43
00:03:30,796 --> 00:03:33,926
He may be my son, but fine.

44
00:03:34,966 --> 00:03:39,606
I will prepare your memorial meals for the rest of my life.

45
00:04:05,896 --> 00:04:07,166
I had never resented my late parents...

46
00:04:08,596 --> 00:04:13,466
for passing away so early as much as I did that night, Mother.

47
00:04:14,266 --> 00:04:18,406
I truly had nowhere to go, and nowhere I wanted to go.

48
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:21,646
I just did not want to live anymore.

49
00:04:35,686 --> 00:04:39,296
Of course I thought about Gang Nam and Dae Chi.

50
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:41,666
They are my own flesh and blood.

51
00:04:59,586 --> 00:05:01,146
Ma'am.

52
00:05:01,216 --> 00:05:04,256
It is dangerous to go into the water at night.

53
00:05:04,656 --> 00:05:06,486
Come down quickly.

54
00:05:08,086 --> 00:05:11,596
I am fine, kid. Just mind your own business and go.

55
00:05:12,196 --> 00:05:15,426
No. Please come down right now.

56
00:05:19,196 --> 00:05:20,236
Unbelievable.

57
00:05:25,206 --> 00:05:27,446
Hey, stop crying.

58
00:05:27,806 --> 00:05:29,846
I came down, so it is fine now.

59
00:05:30,646 --> 00:05:31,646
Okay.

60
00:05:32,646 --> 00:05:35,346
I will give you a good job sticker.

61
00:05:36,956 --> 00:05:37,956
What?

62
00:05:47,126 --> 00:05:49,266
Now go find your mom.

63
00:05:51,066 --> 00:05:53,566
Why would anyone let a young child wander around alone?

64
00:06:01,346 --> 00:06:03,176
Could you let go of me?

65
00:06:05,116 --> 00:06:06,516
I said go to your mom.

66
00:06:11,486 --> 00:06:13,856
Sweetie, why are you all alone?

67
00:06:17,726 --> 00:06:19,196
Ma'am.

68
00:06:19,696 --> 00:06:21,226
I'm hungry.

69
00:06:21,966 --> 00:06:24,266
You didn't eat dinner either?

70
00:06:27,806 --> 00:06:28,866
Oh, my.

71
00:06:30,676 --> 00:06:32,606
If I had not met Da Mi that day,

72
00:06:33,846 --> 00:06:35,746
I would not be in this world anymore.

73
00:07:00,266 --> 00:07:02,136
- Jin Sook? - Go ahead.

74
00:07:02,636 --> 00:07:04,536
Let's meet up.

75
00:07:05,206 --> 00:07:07,576
You abandoned your family and washed your past clean.

76
00:07:07,646 --> 00:07:08,875
It's been a while,

77
00:07:08,876 --> 00:07:11,116
so I want to see the tramp who ran away to save herself.

78
00:07:11,976 --> 00:07:14,516
Is that you, Do Yun's mother?

79
00:07:16,286 --> 00:07:17,716
- Jin Sook. - What?

80
00:07:17,786 --> 00:07:19,086
Hey, Jeon Jin Sook.

81
00:07:19,156 --> 00:07:21,156
Mother, you're up?

82
00:07:22,356 --> 00:07:23,356
Yes.

83
00:07:23,596 --> 00:07:24,826
(Aunt)

84
00:07:25,696 --> 00:07:28,226
Who is calling this late at night?

85
00:07:33,406 --> 00:07:34,406
Oh, yes, Mother.

86
00:07:36,376 --> 00:07:38,106
I'll call you tomorrow when I get to the office.

87
00:07:42,606 --> 00:07:44,176
Did you wake up from your sleep?

88
00:07:44,616 --> 00:07:46,486
I must have fallen asleep early.

89
00:07:48,386 --> 00:07:51,586
- I asked who was on the phone. - Right.

90
00:07:53,626 --> 00:07:55,086
It was an employee from work.

91
00:07:55,456 --> 00:07:56,456
"Jeon Jin Sook?"

92
00:07:57,856 --> 00:08:00,496
Is Jeon Jin Sook someone from your company?

93
00:08:02,666 --> 00:08:04,266
Yes, Mother.

94
00:08:07,206 --> 00:08:10,206
You shouldn't overwork your people.

95
00:08:10,606 --> 00:08:12,576
Always treat them with respect.

96
00:08:14,006 --> 00:08:15,306
I'll keep that in mind.

97
00:08:16,576 --> 00:08:18,475
Mother, are you feeling hungry?

98
00:08:18,476 --> 00:08:19,746
Should I make you some noodles?

99
00:08:20,286 --> 00:08:21,286
That sounds nice.

100
00:08:26,286 --> 00:08:28,086
Your hands are cold.

101
00:08:29,226 --> 00:08:30,226
Let's go inside.

102
00:09:11,436 --> 00:09:12,436
Honey.

103
00:09:17,976 --> 00:09:20,306
You should have stayed in bed. Why did you come out?

104
00:09:20,646 --> 00:09:23,676
This is bad. You said you had an early morning meeting tomorrow.

105
00:09:23,976 --> 00:09:24,976
You weren't next to me.

106
00:09:25,046 --> 00:09:26,816
How could I sleep when I felt so empty?

107
00:09:28,616 --> 00:09:30,116
She must have woken up again.

108
00:09:31,416 --> 00:09:32,486
Do you want some too?

109
00:09:33,486 --> 00:09:35,156
Only if you don't tease me about getting a belly.

110
00:09:35,226 --> 00:09:37,826
Oh, you. Why would I tease you?

111
00:09:53,076 --> 00:09:54,176
It's good, right, Mother?

112
00:09:55,876 --> 00:09:57,376
It's edible.

113
00:09:58,376 --> 00:10:01,046
She put a lot of effort into making it.

114
00:10:02,816 --> 00:10:04,816
I don't want you to get indigestion, Mother.

115
00:10:04,986 --> 00:10:05,986
Please have some water.

116
00:10:09,486 --> 00:10:10,896
Officer.

117
00:10:12,256 --> 00:10:16,536
Ma'am. My son Jun Sung...

118
00:10:16,596 --> 00:10:18,766
and my eldest daughter-in-law...

119
00:10:18,836 --> 00:10:21,766
died in a car accident on the exact same day.

120
00:10:23,236 --> 00:10:25,406
Oh, yes, well.

121
00:10:25,606 --> 00:10:28,446
You must be so devastated, ma'am.

122
00:10:28,506 --> 00:10:32,576
My eldest son was such a good driver.

123
00:10:33,186 --> 00:10:36,046
They said the accident happened because he was a bad driver.

124
00:10:36,486 --> 00:10:39,656
Oh, my. You must be heartbroken.

125
00:10:40,556 --> 00:10:41,986
I mean, well...

126
00:10:42,056 --> 00:10:44,526
Should we give her more sleeping pills?

127
00:10:45,326 --> 00:10:47,626
Let's consult with Dr. Ju first when he gets here.

128
00:10:48,666 --> 00:10:51,096
Ma'am. Officer.

129
00:10:51,236 --> 00:10:52,496
Yes, ma'am.

130
00:10:52,566 --> 00:10:56,836
My eldest son was a really good driver.

131
00:10:57,336 --> 00:11:00,146
Yes, so it's just...

132
00:11:00,676 --> 00:11:02,746
They say when a child dies,

133
00:11:02,806 --> 00:11:06,276
their parents bury them in their hearts,

134
00:11:06,886 --> 00:11:08,386
but that's all a lie.

135
00:11:08,946 --> 00:11:10,516
Not for me.

136
00:11:11,056 --> 00:11:12,516
I see him everywhere I go.

137
00:11:13,186 --> 00:11:14,956
I see him in everything I do.

138
00:11:15,426 --> 00:11:17,356
- Goodness. - Mother.

139
00:11:18,356 --> 00:11:20,396
I will take better care of you.

140
00:11:21,366 --> 00:11:24,896
Yes, Mother. You have us by your side.

141
00:11:24,966 --> 00:11:28,006
Seung Yun, Do Yun, and Se Na, too.

142
00:11:45,556 --> 00:11:46,686
Seriously.

143
00:11:47,786 --> 00:11:48,786
Take this.

144
00:11:51,096 --> 00:11:53,066
No, I'm fine.

145
00:11:53,826 --> 00:11:54,966
Please take this.

146
00:11:56,196 --> 00:11:57,866
I said no, so why do you keep doing this?

147
00:11:58,266 --> 00:11:59,395
You did this earlier too,

148
00:11:59,396 --> 00:12:00,906
and you think money solves everything?

149
00:12:02,306 --> 00:12:03,576
What a strange woman.

150
00:12:04,476 --> 00:12:06,806
I mean, I apologised when I first met her...

151
00:12:06,876 --> 00:12:08,746
and tried to pay her back. That should have been enough.

152
00:12:08,806 --> 00:12:09,946
What more could I do?

153
00:12:10,846 --> 00:12:12,346
What exactly did I do wrong?

154
00:12:14,246 --> 00:12:15,246
CEO Jeon?

155
00:12:18,286 --> 00:12:20,555
- Hi, Team Leader Cha. - I was looking around the stores...

156
00:12:20,556 --> 00:12:22,226
and stopped by because I heard you were here.

157
00:12:26,156 --> 00:12:29,166
- What is going on? - If you are really that curious,

158
00:12:29,226 --> 00:12:31,366
you should ask your boss directly.

159
00:12:32,796 --> 00:12:35,236
What on earth happened with my mom earlier today?

160
00:12:44,176 --> 00:12:45,416
Hey.

161
00:12:46,146 --> 00:12:48,816
Is your company's CEO that great?

162
00:12:49,246 --> 00:12:53,956
How dare she slap my precious junior?

163
00:13:22,386 --> 00:13:24,556
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

164
00:13:30,296 --> 00:13:31,296
Goodness.

165
00:13:41,336 --> 00:13:42,766
Why did he even come?

166
00:13:57,916 --> 00:13:59,756
Goodness, did you sleep well?

167
00:14:04,296 --> 00:14:05,556
Happy birthday, honey.

168
00:14:06,996 --> 00:14:08,396
There's nothing here.

169
00:14:08,466 --> 00:14:10,566
You woke up too early.

170
00:14:13,336 --> 00:14:15,436
Here, I am making seaweed soup.

171
00:14:17,436 --> 00:14:19,206
Are you not being too harsh?

172
00:14:19,536 --> 00:14:21,206
Happy birthday, Dad.

173
00:14:21,506 --> 00:14:22,946
I can just send you some allowance later, right?

174
00:14:23,316 --> 00:14:25,416
Yes, my daughter is the best.

175
00:14:26,516 --> 00:14:29,116
You also have a wife making seaweed soup bright and early.

176
00:14:29,816 --> 00:14:31,986
Of course, even though it is a meal kit.

177
00:14:33,456 --> 00:14:35,685
You should be thankful you have a wife...

178
00:14:35,686 --> 00:14:37,196
who even makes you a meal kit.

179
00:14:37,456 --> 00:14:40,326
Who was the reason we had to move to that old villa in that neighbourhood?

180
00:14:40,396 --> 00:14:42,326
Please. If anyone heard you,

181
00:14:42,396 --> 00:14:44,496
they would think I spent all the money I earned by myself.

182
00:14:44,936 --> 00:14:46,096
Just hurry up and give me food.

183
00:14:46,866 --> 00:14:48,336
They say if you starve on your birthday,

184
00:14:48,406 --> 00:14:50,206
you will have bad luck for one year.

185
00:14:50,706 --> 00:14:53,206
Mom, do we really have to move?

186
00:14:53,576 --> 00:14:56,976
- If I get a loan... - Hey! Absolutely not.

187
00:14:57,346 --> 00:14:58,376
As parents who didn't do much for you,

188
00:14:58,446 --> 00:14:59,986
we can't pass down debt to you, too.

189
00:15:02,286 --> 00:15:06,016
Sweetie, are you not eating with us? It is your dad's birthday.

190
00:15:06,086 --> 00:15:07,686
I have a meeting early in the morning.

191
00:15:07,826 --> 00:15:08,826
Really?

192
00:15:12,156 --> 00:15:13,156
Here.

193
00:15:14,266 --> 00:15:17,066
The rice is in the rice cooker. Hey, Ye Ri, sweetie.

194
00:15:18,136 --> 00:15:19,906
Seriously.

195
00:15:28,706 --> 00:15:30,446
Darn it.

196
00:15:30,776 --> 00:15:32,646
Kang Hak Sung, you man,

197
00:15:32,716 --> 00:15:34,716
your life has really turned out great.

198
00:15:41,926 --> 00:15:44,596
I wonder if Mi Mi had seaweed soup yesterday.

199
00:15:46,866 --> 00:15:50,096
Then again, I am sure the kids took good care of her.

200
00:15:56,066 --> 00:15:59,206
So where did CEO Jeon want to meet you alone?

201
00:15:59,276 --> 00:16:00,446
When is the date?

202
00:16:00,506 --> 00:16:02,806
She asked me to pick a date soon and let her know in advance.

203
00:16:04,646 --> 00:16:06,616
Set a date quickly while she is still interested.

204
00:16:06,686 --> 00:16:08,246
This is a green light for you. You know that, right?

205
00:16:08,316 --> 00:16:09,886
I know.

206
00:16:09,956 --> 00:16:11,986
But what should I wear?

207
00:16:12,056 --> 00:16:13,726
They say a barber can't cut his own hair,

208
00:16:13,786 --> 00:16:15,356
and my daughter is no exception.

209
00:16:15,426 --> 00:16:17,226
You have to wear the newest arrivals from the department store.

210
00:16:18,926 --> 00:16:20,926
My credit card still has some limit left.

211
00:16:21,496 --> 00:16:23,766
Let's meet at the department store after you get off work tonight.

212
00:16:23,836 --> 00:16:25,066
We need to buy you some clothes right away, okay?

213
00:16:26,336 --> 00:16:28,606
You are confident, right, sweetie?

214
00:16:28,666 --> 00:16:30,576
You said Team Leader Cha didn't seem to dislike you.

215
00:16:30,636 --> 00:16:32,136
Yes, I did.

216
00:16:32,206 --> 00:16:33,876
I'm going to make him fall for me, starting now.

217
00:16:34,506 --> 00:16:37,216
Oh, that is my girl.

218
00:16:38,246 --> 00:16:39,716
I promised you.

219
00:16:39,776 --> 00:16:42,986
I told you I would make you so rich you can spend money in your sleep.

220
00:16:43,456 --> 00:16:44,456
Yes.

221
00:16:46,416 --> 00:16:48,326
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

222
00:16:49,326 --> 00:16:50,556
Here you go.

223
00:16:50,896 --> 00:16:52,856
Did your daughter-in-law give birth?

224
00:16:53,866 --> 00:16:56,596
Yes, she is recovering right now.

225
00:16:56,666 --> 00:16:58,496
My husband and I are going to eat quickly...

226
00:16:58,566 --> 00:17:00,866
and take some chicken soup to go for her.

227
00:17:02,206 --> 00:17:03,266
A boy?

228
00:17:03,536 --> 00:17:04,536
It is a girl.

229
00:17:06,036 --> 00:17:07,176
Congratulations.

230
00:17:07,246 --> 00:17:10,616
Daughters treat their parents to nice vacations these days.

231
00:17:11,746 --> 00:17:13,216
The sun is going to set.

232
00:17:13,546 --> 00:17:16,486
Why aren't you bringing out the food quickly?

233
00:17:16,546 --> 00:17:18,416
This is driving me crazy.

234
00:17:18,486 --> 00:17:20,586
I told her we would be busy early today...

235
00:17:20,656 --> 00:17:23,286
and told her not to leave. Gosh.

236
00:17:25,256 --> 00:17:26,256
Here.

237
00:17:26,796 --> 00:17:29,826
Goodness. Here are two ginseng chicken soups.

238
00:17:32,596 --> 00:17:34,566
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

239
00:17:34,636 --> 00:17:37,476
Come again. Thank you as always.

240
00:17:37,536 --> 00:17:39,336
Yes, we enjoyed the meal.

241
00:17:39,406 --> 00:17:41,746
- Keep up the good work. - Yes.

242
00:17:41,806 --> 00:17:45,116
Soon Deok, I am going to take a ten-minute break.

243
00:17:45,576 --> 00:17:47,346
My face is going to roast.

244
00:17:47,846 --> 00:17:49,586
You worked hard all by yourself.

245
00:17:50,056 --> 00:17:51,556
But where did Mi Mi go?

246
00:17:52,086 --> 00:17:54,156
Oh, right, did you not know?

247
00:17:54,226 --> 00:17:57,156
She said Gang Nam and Dae Chi were not answering their phones,

248
00:17:57,226 --> 00:17:59,056
and she tossed and turned all night.

249
00:17:59,256 --> 00:18:00,566
She went to Su Ah's house.

250
00:18:00,626 --> 00:18:03,196
She packed a bunch of side dishes and left at dawn.

251
00:18:03,466 --> 00:18:05,836
She never listens to me.

252
00:18:05,896 --> 00:18:09,236
I told her so many times not to coddle them.

253
00:18:09,306 --> 00:18:11,176
They say the Choi family is stubborn, right?

254
00:18:11,236 --> 00:18:14,876
Our family is also known for being stubborn.

255
00:18:15,606 --> 00:18:18,916
Oh? You didn't tear off the calendar page today.

256
00:18:19,916 --> 00:18:21,486
I should.

257
00:18:21,546 --> 00:18:23,416
I've been so busy since this morning.

258
00:18:23,486 --> 00:18:25,416
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

259
00:18:26,616 --> 00:18:29,126
(July 30)

260
00:18:31,056 --> 00:18:32,096
Darn it.

261
00:18:33,666 --> 00:18:34,866
It's today.

262
00:18:38,636 --> 00:18:39,766
That bastard.

263
00:18:41,736 --> 00:18:44,876
I don't care whether he ate his birthday soup or not.

264
00:19:01,026 --> 00:19:03,356
Why are they still not answering their phones?

265
00:19:24,176 --> 00:19:25,216
This is strange.

266
00:19:26,346 --> 00:19:28,716
Mi Seon should be at home.

267
00:19:32,816 --> 00:19:33,826
Mi Seon.

268
00:19:34,926 --> 00:19:36,086
Su Ah's mom.

269
00:19:39,726 --> 00:19:40,726
Mi Seon.

270
00:19:43,426 --> 00:19:45,636
Hello. I am sorry.

271
00:19:46,166 --> 00:19:47,666
Are they not home?

272
00:19:48,906 --> 00:19:50,606
They moved out a couple of days ago.

273
00:19:51,406 --> 00:19:53,176
Didn't you know?

274
00:19:54,676 --> 00:19:56,376
They moved?

275
00:19:57,016 --> 00:19:58,516
My son and his family?

276
00:20:33,646 --> 00:20:36,986
Well, when you're raising a kid, you can get pretty busy.

277
00:20:39,286 --> 00:20:41,526
Right. Let's just go with that.

278
00:20:47,626 --> 00:20:48,666
These might sour.

279
00:21:37,446 --> 00:21:38,976
Just ten minutes left.

280
00:22:03,806 --> 00:22:05,876
Will I only get this far today, too?

281
00:22:11,046 --> 00:22:12,046
Hey.

282
00:22:12,116 --> 00:22:14,515
Da Mi, CEO Lee from Seungah Construction is here.

283
00:22:14,516 --> 00:22:16,645
He's 20 minutes early for his appointment.

284
00:22:16,646 --> 00:22:18,156
Oh, okay. I'll be right there.

285
00:22:19,216 --> 00:22:22,085
Min Hee. For CEO Lee's hot Americano,

286
00:22:22,086 --> 00:22:24,596
don't forget to put three ice cubes in it, okay?

287
00:22:24,656 --> 00:22:25,926
I'll be right there.

288
00:22:31,896 --> 00:22:34,506
- Where am I? At the mall. - Why?

289
00:22:34,666 --> 00:22:36,536
Please don't tell me you went out to do market research...

290
00:22:36,606 --> 00:22:37,936
as soon as you got back.

291
00:22:38,336 --> 00:22:40,506
Wait. Are you watching me or something?

292
00:22:41,006 --> 00:22:42,046
That's creepy.

293
00:22:43,346 --> 00:22:45,675
So the offer we made to our target, Jaden,

294
00:22:45,676 --> 00:22:47,846
was impossible to turn down like you said.

295
00:22:48,386 --> 00:22:49,616
They want to meet up ASAP.

296
00:22:50,116 --> 00:22:52,386
Yes? I knew it.

297
00:22:53,016 --> 00:22:54,126
Guess I was right.

298
00:22:57,826 --> 00:23:01,266
Jaden, Ms. Chan is coming in pretty aggressively.

299
00:23:01,326 --> 00:23:02,866
What stance should we take?

300
00:23:03,266 --> 00:23:04,466
Any suggestions?

301
00:23:10,676 --> 00:23:12,976
Jaden? Hey, Seung Yun.

302
00:23:13,276 --> 00:23:14,346
My boss.

303
00:23:14,646 --> 00:23:16,406
My bad. Sorry. One second.

304
00:23:21,916 --> 00:23:24,716
Go with the original plan. No changes.

305
00:23:25,956 --> 00:23:26,956
That's all.

306
00:23:29,756 --> 00:23:31,226
Okay, got it.

307
00:23:31,296 --> 00:23:32,556
Talk soon. Bye.

308
00:23:46,376 --> 00:23:48,106
- Here you go. - Thanks.

309
00:23:55,646 --> 00:23:58,456
Da Mi, I'm going to run to the pharmacy real quick.

310
00:23:59,516 --> 00:24:01,185
- You must be in a lot of pain. - Yes.

311
00:24:01,186 --> 00:24:04,326
I forgot to bring my medicine today too. Hurry back.

312
00:24:04,396 --> 00:24:07,026
- You really suffer every month. - I'm sorry.

313
00:24:16,666 --> 00:24:19,336
(Sibling 1)

314
00:24:23,546 --> 00:24:24,815
- Why is my sister-in-law... - The customer you are calling...

315
00:24:24,816 --> 00:24:25,945
- is unavailable... - and my oldest brother...

316
00:24:25,946 --> 00:24:27,416
not answering?

317
00:24:28,416 --> 00:24:30,856
(Sibling 2)

318
00:24:33,086 --> 00:24:34,186
What?

319
00:24:34,786 --> 00:24:37,756
Yesterday was Mom's birthday. Dae Chi, didn't you know?

320
00:24:37,826 --> 00:24:39,756
Gang Nam and his wife didn't show up either.

321
00:24:39,826 --> 00:24:41,766
Do you know how bad I felt?

322
00:24:44,666 --> 00:24:46,596
- Da Mi. - What's wrong with you?

323
00:24:46,666 --> 00:24:48,366
You're actually saying my name so sweetly.

324
00:24:48,966 --> 00:24:52,706
- I asked why you didn't come. - I was crazy busy with work.

325
00:24:55,106 --> 00:24:56,306
By the way, do you have any savings?

326
00:24:56,676 --> 00:24:57,676
Excuse me?

327
00:24:57,746 --> 00:24:59,616
You're a successful manager at a big company.

328
00:24:59,676 --> 00:25:01,086
You're a cheapskate.

329
00:25:01,246 --> 00:25:03,346
How much have you saved up? It's a lot, right?

330
00:25:03,416 --> 00:25:07,016
Probably less than you. Call Mom right now...

331
00:25:07,086 --> 00:25:08,356
and buy her a gift.

332
00:25:11,526 --> 00:25:14,526
I'm already struggling just to get by because of money.

333
00:25:14,826 --> 00:25:16,366
How much have I saved?

334
00:25:17,796 --> 00:25:19,295
Does he think everyone makes as much as he does...

335
00:25:19,296 --> 00:25:20,666
just because they have a job?

336
00:25:21,366 --> 00:25:23,436
A penny saved is just a penny.

337
00:25:24,906 --> 00:25:27,476
Wait. Oh, right. Gosh.

338
00:25:29,976 --> 00:25:31,276
My hard-earned money.

339
00:25:33,676 --> 00:25:38,256
Kim Pro. You bastard!

340
00:25:49,226 --> 00:25:50,226
What?

341
00:25:56,566 --> 00:25:58,436
This is completely bizarre.

342
00:26:00,976 --> 00:26:02,146
Who did this?

343
00:26:12,286 --> 00:26:15,226
(Mission: Mompossible)

344
00:26:39,316 --> 00:26:40,346
Mi Mi.

345
00:26:40,416 --> 00:26:44,256
I just keep liking you more and more.

346
00:26:44,316 --> 00:26:46,386
The more I see you, the more I like you.

347
00:26:46,656 --> 00:26:48,286
I'll do even better, Mother.

348
00:26:48,626 --> 00:26:51,356
- Jin Sook! - What do you want?

349
00:26:51,596 --> 00:26:52,956
I'll send you my account number,

350
00:26:53,026 --> 00:26:55,696
- so wire it by tomorrow. - This is the last time.

351
00:26:56,266 --> 00:26:58,236
You must be thrilled, Grandma.

352
00:26:58,436 --> 00:27:01,536
You are all my beautiful grandchildren,

353
00:27:01,606 --> 00:27:03,406
but the eldest grandson is different.

354
00:27:03,606 --> 00:27:07,176
He is the central root and the pillar of this family.

355
00:27:07,506 --> 00:27:08,706
This is just the beginning.

356
00:27:09,146 --> 00:27:10,916
I will uncover the truth.

357
00:27:11,576 --> 00:27:13,846
What are you doing here?

358
00:27:14,146 --> 00:27:16,886
- Oh, my gosh! - Wait, why is this here...

359
00:27:16,946 --> 00:27:17,956
Please give it to me.

360
00:27:19,516 --> 00:27:21,056
Yes, of course.

361
00:27:28,296 --> 00:27:29,496
(Mission: Mompossible)
